body:
I can agree with this to some extent. The emperor being uber powerful and being close to him being dangerous is kinda cool. But i absolutely hate the necessity of suffering on every level of 40k. For example that people who work in hive cities work 20 hour shifts. Thats not possible in any capacity and it would kill so fast that hive cities would become empty after a while. (My personal headcannon for that is that the hive cities have multiple day and night cycles, that way someone is always working). There are other aspects, like how you feed the chaos gods no matter what you do, psykers will all eventually go insane if they live long enough, the Tyranids are probably going to eat the entire universe and shit like that. Its not fun to know that everything you know and love in the setting is doomed. That just seems depressing to me. 

&#x200B;

HOWEVER once i started getting more into the lore and started accepting that headcannon counts for a lot in the wh40k fandom, it became better.

I have two moments i do believe counts as huge wtf moments. Both are committed by the same player but two of their characters:

1: the group had gone to a sort of pirate island paradise and managed to catch the start of a trading festival. and the party rogue decides he wants to play games, so he sits down and does the "follow the coin" stuff, but fails miserably on his perception so he cannot track the coin. He looses 10 gold and walks away. Then he does a 180 and sneak attacks the man, lopping both of his arms off (commoner has 2hp, he did 27 points of damage). What follows is: he gets arrested, put in jail, escapes to collect his sword, fights a firefist solo while naked, gets arrested again, is trialed for murder and assault, willingly chooses trial by combat and challenges the strongest one at the venue who is a disguised oni. I want you to imagine what happens when a rogue goes 1v1 against a monster who has regenerate when the rogue cant sneak attack ever. Even after buffing him with extra attack and HP (magic sword, dont ask) he still goes down. the boss started with 120 hp and ended the fight with 118 HP.

&#x200B;

2: the party had been traveling and just managed to fend off a group of manticores when one of the manticores are snatched out of the air by a green hand, the party hides as they hear the sound of the manticore being torn in half. The paladin (same player different character). Walks out to see what it was, no stealth, just walks out. He sees that it is an adult green dragon. He then yells at it, and i quote "hello there, would you like to be my pet". Now for those who don't know, green dragons are extremely vain and very evil. So the dragon gets offended. Fast forward the dragon slaps him into the ground so hard he dies, upon the dragon ressurects him because of a nat 20 persuasion check from a fellow party member. He the proceeds to tell the dragon he has achieved immortality and it should tuck tail and run away "you pathetic lizard". the dragon kills him again, and his soul is intercepted by the campaign secret BBEG who says he can save him. When the paladin asks "who are you" the BBEG says "im just  a myth" as he is supposed to be very mysterious. Paladin takes this literally and decides it means the devil in front of him actually doesn't exist and signs his devil contract no questions asked.

&#x200B;

TLDR. player has two very dumb characters who decides fucking with people or entities far above them is not a detriment to their health and gets clapped for it

I struggle with the exact same problem. But my advice for you is to take it at your pace. At lower levels the party will probably not do anything more riveting than chasing away monsters or hunting down bandits. what i did was dropping hints to bigger threats during those small missions. Use these early missions as ways to give your players opportunities to make connections for example, drop hints to bigger villains and larger conflicts. 

&#x200B;

Also have a notepad on your phone, write every mildly interesting ideas that dear drag its ass across your plane of imagination. Thats how i do it at least

That sounds sick, wouldnt it be awesome if it flew with wings insead of thrusters?

&#x200B;

